/// CENTRAL 25-C §1a — the two-tier membership model.
///
/// ⚠⚠ THIS IS NOT A ROLE AND DOES NOT LIVE ON THE SAME AXIS AS ONE. A tier says
/// how somebody got into the Community; a role says what they may do on one
/// node. A branch member can be the OWNER of their branch (BRANCH + OWNER) and
/// a group member can be an ordinary MEMBER of the root (GROUP + MEMBER).
///
///   GROUP  — invited at top level. May found a branch and become its manager;
///            may invite at top level; may invite into branches.
///   BRANCH — invited into one branch, and holds a root membership only because
///            Stage 1.2's branch-implies-root rule creates one. May invite
///            others into that branch. May NOT found a branch or invite at top
///            level.
enum CommunityMembershipTier {
  GROUP
  BRANCH
}

